module CollapsedContainerTrailingComment exposing (..)

-- "Does this container render multi-line?" -- which decides whether a trailing
-- block comment may glue onto its closing bracket's row -- is the container's
-- own STORED box type, not its source row span.
--
-- The two disagree on exactly the containers that COLLAPSE. `authoredBracketList`
-- builds an `AllAcrossOrAllVertical` when `itemsSpanRows` is False, and a
-- single-item container can never have a gap *between* items, so `[ 1` / `]`
-- renders `[ 1 ]` on one row (divergence #21) while its row range still spans
-- the two rows the author used. `bracketRendersMultiline` read the range,
-- promised a glue row the output does not have, and the comment moved to its own
-- row on the second format. Reading the box type instead is subtractive: the
-- author-intent flag was already computed, stored and right.
--
-- A formatter-SYNTHESIZED paren (a type or pattern wrap) is the same story with
-- the same fix: it carries no author position, so its `forceVertical` is False
-- and it renders flat however the author broke it.
--
-- Found by `matrix-syntax.py --comments` on the multi-line comment kind
-- (2026-08-05): 54 cells, ~48 of them the paren arm.


oneItemArray =
    [ 1 ]
{- multi
   second row -}


oneFieldRecord =
    { a = 1 }
{- multi
   second row -}


oneItemArrayAsCallArg =
    fn a
        [ 1 ]
        {- multi
           second row -}
        last


-- THE BOUNDARY. A container the author genuinely broke BETWEEN items keeps its
-- `AlwaysVertical` box, renders across rows, and its closing bracket is a row a
-- trailing comment still glues onto.


twoItemArrayStillGlues =
    [ 1
    , 2
    ] {- multi
         second row -}


twoFieldRecordStillGlues =
    { a = 1
    , b = 2
    } {- multi
         second row -}


-- An author-written paren carries `forceVertical` of its own, so it is unmoved
-- either way: broken across rows it renders its `)` on its own line and the
-- comment glues onto that row.


brokenParenStillGlues =
    (one
    ) {- multi
         second row -}
